course: dictionary
lesson: 1970
title: Complaints and context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A complaint is a statement that something is wrong or not good enough. Context helps you spot it. «Bit by bit its eyes and its head appear, and Alice tells it all her complaints.» Alice is telling the creature everything that is wrong, so a complaint is a list of things a person is unhappy about.
explain: The same word can mean different things. «In 2013 Mid Devon council tried a similar ban and changed its mind after complaints.» Here, people told the council they were unhappy, and the council listened. Ask: what would fit here? Try «reports of what was wrong» in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Complaint can also mean an illness. «A common complaint» means an illness that many people get. How do you know? The word common, and the fact that people are not making a statement about a shop or a council. Read the words around the word, then check your meaning.
fact: A complaint is a statement that something is wrong or not good enough.
fact: A complaint can also be a reason for being unhappy.
fact: «Make a complaint» means to tell someone officially that something is wrong.
fact: In health, a complaint is an illness or health problem, as in «a common complaint».
fact: In 2013 Mid Devon council changed its mind after complaints from people.
exercise: «Bit by bit its eyes and its head appear, and Alice tells it all her complaints.» What is a complaint in this sentence? | A kind present for the creature | A song the creature likes | A game that Alice invents | *Things that Alice says are wrong
exercise: «In 2013 Mid Devon council changed its mind after complaints.» What were the complaints? | Plans for a new park | Compliments about the signs | Letters asking for a holiday | *Statements that something was wrong
exercise: What does «make a complaint» mean? | To fall fast asleep | *To tell someone officially that something is wrong | To make a cake for a friend | To be happy with a gift
test: «A common complaint» means what? | A nice remark about someone | *An illness or health problem | A bad mood for just one day | A type of music
test: «One complaint is not a pattern; get facts before you warn people off a business.» What is the best meaning? | Complaints always come in threes | *One person's complaint is not yet a trend, so check the facts first | Close the business at once because one person spoke | Only happy customers ever write letters
exam: Which word means a statement that something is wrong, not a nice remark? | pattern | celebration | compliment | *complaint
